/* c.Cache - LanManFS cache module.
 *
 * Implementation of the cache module declared in h.Cache: the FNV-1a
 * hash with ASCII-only case fold, the slab and free-list management,
 * the list sentinel discipline, the SRHeap-backed string and content
 * heaps, the read path, directory enumeration and its listings, file
 * content kept from whole loads and captured through open handles,
 * the mutation hook bodies and the open-file handle table.
 *
 * The cache makes no SWI calls, and its RISC OS headers sit behind
 * the RISCOS seam below, so it also builds and runs on Linux
 * as it does under Norcroft.  Time is read via a caller-supplied function
 * pointer; on RISC OS the module passes its centisecond tick, and a
 * test build on Linux passes a deterministic counter.
 */

